{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our ADK agent on Cloud Run is double-reporting spans in Cloud Trace. every LLM call shows up twice, once under the agent span and once floating at root level. we added OpenTelemetry manually before realizing ADK already emits some stuff. also some tool calls don't show up at all?? how do I get one clean trace per conversation turn"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Hi — we're about 3 weeks out from handing our customer-support agent (ADK, deployed on Agent Engine, Gemini 2.5 Flash + a couple of BigQuery tools) over to the client's IT ops team. Right now the only way we know something's wrong is when their product manager pings us on Slack. Before handover I'd like: per-conversation token cost we can actually report on, alerts when p95 latency or our eval scores drop, and some kind of runbook their team can follow to pull up a single bad conversation and figure out what happened. Last week we had a session where the agent looped on a tool call 40 times and nobody noticed for a day, so I also need to write a postmortem on that. Where do I start?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "the agent is super slow in prod, like 12-15s per response, users are complaining. it's an ADK SequentialAgent with 4 sub-agents each calling gemini-2.5-pro. we already have tracing set up and I can see exactly where the time goes, it's just the model calls stacking up. how do I make it faster", "needs_instead": "Performance and architecture help: restructuring the agent (parallel sub-agents, smaller/faster models for some steps, fewer sequential LLM calls, streaming responses). Their visibility already works, so this isn't a monitoring problem."}
]}
